unresolved.message:
@Emily Wachowiak This option felt much easier to skim. 

* I like that the headline really calls out the 3 areas that are in the new section (it reads real snappy!) 
* I don't mind the "when available" in the parentheses and in fact, OPO, makes it even easier to read!

From my comment above:

@Megan Daniel if it would be functioning as a banner and would still allow a user to interact with the rest of the page, we could follow the tidbit pattern (a group with CTAs), especially if we expect there won't be more than 2 action buttons.

The Banner could follow the tidbit pattern: https://www.magentaa11y.com/checklist-native/tidbit/ - a group with an accessible label but not restricting the user's interaction with the rest of the page.

